<%# The `.editing` class normally lives on the grid wrapper that `edit-mode`
    toggles; here it is hard-coded so a single card can be inspected in both
    states.

    The box has to match the CELL the size actually occupies in the bento, or
    the preview lies about the layout: the grid is `auto-rows-[16rem]` with a
    `gap-4`, so a two-row size is 16 + 1 + 16 = 33rem tall, not 16. This used to
    be a flat `lg:h-64` for every size, which squeezed `large` and `wide` into
    one row and clipped their charts — the card was fine and the preview was
    wrong, which is the worse of the two failures because it sends you looking
    in the component. %>
<%
  height = case size
           when :large then 'lg:h-[33rem]'
           else 'lg:h-64'
           end
  width = case size
          when :small then 'max-w-xs'
          else 'max-w-md'
          end
%>
<div class="<%= 'editing' if editing %> <%= width %> p-8">
  <div class="<%= height %>">
    <%= render Bali::Widget::Component.new(widget, size: size) %>
  </div>
</div>
